# This project is developed on both macOS and Windows. Without a policy here,
# Git for Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` can commit CRLF endings, and the
# two machines then see whole files as modified when nothing has changed.
#
# Normalise everything to LF in the repository. Editors on Windows handle LF
# fine; this only controls what is stored.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must keep LF even if a tool would rather not.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.db binary
*.dump binary

# SQL dumps are text but large and machine-generated; keeping them out of diffs
# makes reviews readable.
*.sql -diff

# Lockfiles are generated. Marking them keeps them out of diff noise if one is
# ever committed.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
